   "translation": {
    "literal": "Keśava I satisfy. Nārāyaṇa I satisfy. Mādhava I satisfy. Govinda I satisfy. Viṣṇu I satisfy. Madhusūdana I satisfy. Trivikrama I satisfy. Vāmana I satisfy. Śrīdhara I satisfy. Hṛṣīkeśa I satisfy. Padmanābha I satisfy. Dāmodara I satisfy.",
    "readable": "I offer water to Keśava, Nārāyaṇa, Mādhava, Govinda, Viṣṇu, Madhusūdana, Trivikrama, Vāmana, Śrīdhara, Hṛṣīkeśa, Padmanābha and Dāmodara."
   }
  }
 ],
 "meaning": "The same twelve names of Viṣṇu that were said at the ācamana (anga-vandana), now in the accusative, each receiving water with ‘I satisfy’. With the nine grahas before them they make the tarpaṇa of the Sandhyāvandanam, after which the ācamana closes the first part of the rite.",
 "in_the_rite": "Step tarpana, after the nine grahas, in all three services; then the ācamana that ends the first part (pūrvabhāga) of the rite.",
